---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Lu Zhang / SciencesLoop"
  description="Privacy policy for Lu Zhang's personal site, SciencesLoop developer application, and property operations SMS support."
>
  <div class="container" style="padding-top: 3rem; max-width: 820px;">
    <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This policy covers Lu Zhang's personal site and the SciencesLoop
      LinkedIn developer application. It also covers property operations SMS
      support used for message recipients, applicants, service providers, and
      operations contacts.
    </p>

    <h2>Information Collected</h2>
    <p>
      This public site does not require account registration and does not
      intentionally collect sensitive personal information. Standard hosting,
      browser, and server logs may record basic technical information such as
      page requests, timestamps, browser type, and referring URLs.
    </p>
    <p>
      When the public site agent is enabled, questions submitted to the agent
      may be sent to the configured SciencesLoop API so the service can
      generate an answer from public website content. The agent is not intended
      to access private files or confidential records.
    </p>

    <h2>LinkedIn Application Use</h2>
    <p>
      SciencesLoop may use LinkedIn's official authorization flow only when
      the site owner explicitly grants access. The application is intended for
      drafting or publishing owner-approved LinkedIn posts about public
      AI-for-science, scientific-agent, RAG, MLOps, and portfolio content.
    </p>
    <p>
      The application is not intended to scrape LinkedIn profiles, read private
      messages, manage job applications, or publish content without explicit
      owner review.
    </p>

    <h2>Comments</h2>
    <p>
      Article comments, if enabled, may use Giscus, which stores comments in a
      public GitHub Discussions repository and requires a GitHub account to
      post. Comments are loaded only after a reader chooses to load the comment
      widget. When comments are not configured, the site shows direct feedback
      links instead.
    </p>

    <h2>Property Operations SMS</h2>
    <p>
      Zhang Rental Management uses property operations SMS only for
      non-marketing support for existing residential tenants and service
      vendors, including maintenance requests, repair follow-up, appointment
      coordination, lease or parking questions, and vendor scheduling.
    </p>
    <p>
      An existing tenant or service vendor opts in by reviewing the public
      <a href="/property-sms/">SMS consent notice</a> and personally texting
      <strong>START</strong> to the property operations support number. START
      is the only opt-in method for this program. This enrolls the person in
      recurring transactional property operations messages. Consent is not a
      condition of renting or receiving property management services.
    </p>
    <p>
      SMS message content, phone numbers, timestamps, and related support notes
      may be stored as operational records so that service requests can be
      reviewed and handled. These records are not sold and are not shared with
      third parties for marketing purposes.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not share, sell, or otherwise provide mobile phone numbers or
      messaging consent information to any third parties or affiliates for
      marketing or promotional purposes. We may share information with service
      providers only as necessary to deliver and support this text messaging
      service. All other categories of information exclude text messaging
      originator opt-in data and consent.
    </p>
    <p>
      SMS recipients can reply <strong>STOP</strong> to opt out, <strong>START</strong>
      to resubscribe, or <strong>HELP</strong> for assistance.
    </p>
    <p>
      Message frequency varies with the support request. Message and data rates
      may apply.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      This site does not sell personal data. SMS opt-in data and consent are not
      shared with third parties for marketing purposes. Public links may point to
      external services such as Google Scholar, GitHub, LinkedIn, journals,
      patents, and public research records.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions or removal requests, contact
      <a href="mailto:zhanglu77@gmail.com">zhanglu77@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
